# Inherited name-coupling in sh2perl/src — a RATCHET, not an exemption.
#
# docs/GENERAL-GPU-LIFT.md §6 forbids program identifiers in the compiler.
# The tree did not satisfy that rule when the gate landed: c_backend.rs
# carries rasterizer fast paths written against one program (`rb_clear`,
# `rb_putrun`, `rb_present`, `RFB_PIX`, `RFB_ROWS`, an `RBTEX` prefix test,
# one `MIMEcroft` comment that is not a comment line). Those are real debt,
# not interface names — they name the program under compilation.
#
# Format: <file under sh2perl/src> <root> <max lines>
#
# The gate fails when a count EXCEEDS its budget (a new coupling) or when a
# file appears that is not listed here. Counts are per line, classified by
# the first matching root in the order rb_, RBTEX, RFB_, MIME, SCOS, SSIN.
# Removing coupling is always allowed: lower the number in the same commit
# so the ratchet only moves down.
c_backend.rs rb_ 11
c_backend.rs RBTEX 1
c_backend.rs RFB_ 16
c_backend.rs MIME 1
